    "note": "The blind statement is for an arbitrary group G, which is not assumed to be finite. X(sh_G) has 13 elements, and every orbit is finite of a size that divides 8. X(sh_G) is the sum of the underlying sets of the orbits (chapter 5). Orbits are finite subsets of a finite set, so equality of orbits is decidable and X/G is finite. Our finite-family lemma gives an orbit with one element. A G-set with contractible X(sh_G) has a fixed point. The parenthetical remark (|G| = 8) is our gset_orbit_card_divides, transported to the blind orbit sets. These sets are definitionally our GSetOrbitSet."
