    "note": "There are two blind statements: the literal one is about all subgroups, and the corrected one is about decidable subgroups. Both assert the 26-digit count for C_2^18, and neither is derived. Modules 1040-1043 show that the decidable subgroups of any group ≃ the Bool-valued abstract subgroups. Hence they are finite for a finite group. C_2^0, C_2^1 and C_2^2 have 1, 2 and 5 decidable subgroups (bridged in the blind format). The n = 18 count needs the Goldman-Rota recurrence for subspaces of F_2^n and verified non-unary arithmetic. This was not attempted. The literal reading (all subgroups finite in number) is constructively unprovable. Module 1024 shows that the finiteness of all subgroups of finite groups is equivalent to LEM. The asymptotic 7·2^(n^2/4) is not formalized, because it is vague in both readings."
