    "note": "The blind G/H (the underlying set of coker i) is our Bi⁻¹(sh_G), up to the set truncation of a set. Part (2) is bridged: |H| = |G| ⇒ H = G. Here the blind full subgroup is the image of id, which is ours. Part (1) is stated literally for every subgroup, and it includes the finiteness of H and G/H. This literal statement is equivalent to excluded middle. Both directions are proved (bridge_lagrangeascounting_of_lem, bridge_lagrangeascounting_lem, through module 1024). So it is a deliberate gap. It is bridged for finite H (bridge_lagrangeascounting_finite = ours) and under LEM. The book is ambiguous, because its proof asserts the finiteness of H. Our statement assumes that H is finite, and book-inventory.json documents this."
